<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n75120" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὅρκ-ιος</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ον</span>,
		rarely <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">α</span>, <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ον</span>
		<i><span class="en">
			E.
			<u>Med.</u>
			208
		</span></i> (lyr.):—<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>belonging to an oath,</i> i.e. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>1.</b>
			<i>sworn, bound by oath,</i>
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">δικαστὰς ὁ. αἱρουμένη</span> (so
			Casaub.) <i><span class="en">
				A.
				<u>Eu.</u>
				483
			</span></i> ; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὅ. λέγω</span> I speak <i>on
				oath,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				S.
				<u>Ant.</u>
				305
			</span></i>, cf. <i><span class="en">
				<u>OC</u>
				1637
			</span></i>: 
				Comp.
			, <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὁρκιωτέραν δ᾽ ἤμην τὰν
			δώλαν</span> the slave's <i>oath shall carry the greater
				weight,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				Leg.Gort.
				2.15
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b>
			<i>that which is sworn by,</i>
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὅ. θεοί</span> the gods <i>invoked at
				an oath,</i> who watch over its fulfilment and punish its
			violation, <i><span class="en">
				E.
				<u>Ph.</u>
				481
			</span></i>, cf. <i><span class="en">
				<u>IT</u>
				747
			</span></i> : in Prose, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">θεοὶ οἱ ὅ.</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Th.
					1.71
				</span></i>
			,<i><span class="en">
				78
			</span></i> ; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">οἱ ὅ. θ.</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Aeschin.
					1.114
				</span></i>
			 ; esp. 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Ζεὺς ὅ.</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					S.
					<u>Ph.</u>
					1324
				</span></i>
			, <i><span class="en">
				E.
				<u>Hipp.</u>
				1025
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Arist.
				<u>Mir.</u>
				845b33
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Paus.
				5.24.9s
			</span></i>q., etc.; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὁρκία Θέμις</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					E.
					<u>Med.</u>
				</span></i>
			 l.c. ; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">φθιμένων σέβας ὅ.</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					<u>AP</u>
					7.351
				</span></i>
			 (<i><span class="en">
				Diosc.
			</span></i>); <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ξίφος ὅ.</span> a sword
				<i>sworn by,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				E.
				<u>Ph.</u>
				1677
			</span></i>.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
